<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Drift with a current at right angles</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A boat is steered on a course of \([[if test="is(c<99.95)"]]0[[/if]][[if test="is(c<9.95)"]]0[[/if]]{@c@}^\circ\) at \({@v@}\) knots through the water. A current flows towards \([[if test="is(cc<99.95)"]]0[[/if]][[if test="is(cc<9.95)"]]0[[/if]]{@cc@}^\circ\) at \({@u@}\) knots.</p><p>(a) Find the ground speed, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans1]] knots [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the drift angle, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans2]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) Find the track, as a bearing correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans3]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The course is where the boat points; the track is where it goes. Draw the course arrow (\({@v@}\) knots towards \([[if test="is(c<99.95)"]]0[[/if]][[if test="is(c<9.95)"]]0[[/if]]{@c@}^\circ\)), then the current arrow from its tip (\({@u@}\) knots towards \([[if test="is(cc<99.95)"]]0[[/if]][[if test="is(cc<9.95)"]]0[[/if]]{@cc@}^\circ\)). The current is at right angles to the course, so the triangle is right-angled and the track arrow is its hypotenuse.</p><p>(a) Ground speed \(= \sqrt{ {@v@}^2 + {@u@}^2} = {@dispdp(float(gs),3)@} \approx {@dispdp(r1(gs),1)@}\) knots.</p><p>(b) \(\tan d = \dfrac{ {@u@} }{ {@v@} }\), so \(d = {@dispdp(float(dr),3)@}^\circ \approx {@dispdp(r1(dr),1)@}^\circ\).</p><p>(c) The current pushes the boat [[if test="is(sd=1)"]]clockwise[[else]]anticlockwise[[/if]] of its course, so the track is \({@c@}^\circ [[if test="is(sd=1)"]]+[[else]]-[[/if]] {@dispdp(r1(dr),1)@}^\circ[[if test="is(c+sd*dr<0)"]] + 360^\circ[[/if]] = [[if test="is(r1(tr)<99.95)"]]0[[/if]][[if test="is(r1(tr)<9.95)"]]0[[/if]]{@dispdp(float(r1(tr)),1)@}^\circ\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[cosd(x) := cos(x*%pi/180);
sind(x) := sin(x*%pi/180);
atand(x) := 180*atan(x)/%pi;
asind(x) := 180*asin(x)/%pi;
two(v) := if v < 10 then sconcat("0", string(v)) else string(v);
hm(m) := block([q], q: mod(m, 1440), sconcat(two(floor(q/60)), ":", two(mod(q, 60))));
dmx(m) := sconcat(string(floor(m/60)), "^\\circ", two(mod(m, 60)), "'");
cosd(x) := float(cos(x*%pi/180)); sind(x) := float(sin(x*%pi/180));
atand(x) := float(180*atan(x)/%pi); asind(x) := float(180*asin(x)/%pi);
r1(x) := float(floor(10*x+1/2)/10);
clr(x, L) := every(lambda([y], is(abs(x-y)>0.2)), L);
/* Design: crossing with the current at right angles, in knots, with the track as a bearing. The negative-bearing node applies only when the course is 000 and the current pushes anticlockwise; elsewhere neg = -999, a value no bearing takes (used only by its test). Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Mechanics 1, chapter 2, Exercise E questions 3 and 5. */
VU: [[7,3],[8,5],[9,4],[10,3],[12,5],[13,6],[15,7],[16,5],[18,8],[20,7]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
v: VU[ix][1]; u: VU[ix][2];
c: 45*rand(8);
sd: rand([1,-1]);
cc: mod(c+90*sd,360);
gs: sqrt(v^2+u^2);
dr: atand(u/v);
tr: mod(c+sd*dr,360);
/* diagnostics */
sm: v+u; df: v-u; py: sqrt(v^2-u^2);
cmp: 90-dr; asn: asind(u/v);
ws: mod(c-sd*dr,360); tc: mod(c+sd*(90-dr),360);
neg: if c+sd*dr<0 then c+sd*dr else -999;
ra: r1(dr)+3;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
