  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Navigation: drift with a current at right angles</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.7 (f): Find the ground speed, drift angle and track of a boat when the current is at right angles to its course.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 2, Exercise E, questions 3 and 5 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Mechanics 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: crossing with a current at right angles; speeds in knots, the track as a bearing, new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
